==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionRule  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermissionRule.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionRule decouples Operation.outcome from IsPermitted. The injection then asks Alloy to find a Permitted Operation whose (role, opKind) cell (ComplianceOfficer, ReadRecord) is explicitly denied by the matrix — a direct counterexample to LeastPrivilege and the compliance-content-forbidden assertions.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_007_ComplianceContentForbidden, FR_019_ComplianceContentBlindness
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceContentForbidden: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_ComplianceContentBlindness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneAuditPerOperation  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_OneAuditPerOperation.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the one-audit-per-operation constraint. The injection forces an Operation that has no associated AuditEntry, directly contradicting the audit-completeness assertions.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_013_OneAuditPerOperation
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_OneAuditPerOperation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Clearing the attribution fact lets the AuditEntry's accessor field drift from the underlying Operation's actor. The injection forces such a misattributed audit entry into the instance.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_014_AuditFieldsCorrect
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditFieldsCorrect: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteOpLink  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteOpLink.als
    rationale: F_NoteOpLink is the bijection between ClinicalNote and permitted-append Operations. Clearing it lets a 'phantom' note exist with no creating operation — exactly the append-only / provenance violation the AppendOnly assertion is meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_NotesAppendOnly, FR_011_NoteFieldsSnapshot
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoteFieldsSnapshot: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionRule  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermissionRule.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission rule severs the link between Permitted outcomes and the care-team membership precondition. The injection forces a clinician to be granted a Permitted ReadRecord on a record they are NOT on the care team for — the canonical ownership/care-team violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteOpLink  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteOpLink.als
    rationale: Clearing F_NoteOpLink decouples a Denied operation from its (forbidden) side effects. The injection forces a Denied operation that nonetheless produced a clinical note — a state change leaking through the byte-equivalent 403 envelope.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_008_ByteEquivalentDenied
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_ByteEquivalentDenied: FAIL (expected)

